mixin () {
  /// Static Markdown description of this canister's public API.
  public query func getApiDoc() : async Text {
    let doc : Text = "\23 Tuition Class Attendance API\n\nBackend for a personal tuition-class attendance tracker. Each signed-in user\nowns their own subjects (class tabs) and the attendance records attached to\nthem. All data is scoped to the caller's principal.\n\n\23\23 Authentication\n\nEvery method below requires a signed (non-anonymous) caller. The app's frontend\npins an Internet Identity derivation origin, published at\n`/.well-known/ii-derivation-origin` when available; an agent already holding the\nuser's Internet Identity authorization derives the correct per-app principal\nagainst that origin (for example `icp identity link web <name> --app <host>`).\nSuch a delegation acts with the user's full authority in this app until it\nexpires.\n\nThis canister uses the Caffeine authorization component. A caller that has never\nsigned in through the app's own frontend is unregistered even when it belongs to\nthe app's owner, and a signed-in caller derived against a different origin is a\ndifferent principal than the one the frontend registered. Register a direct API\ncaller by calling `_initialize_access_control` once as a signed-in caller before\nany role-guarded call, including guarded queries. The first initializer receives\nthe `admin` role; subsequent callers receive the `user` role. An unregistered or\nanonymous caller on a guarded endpoint is rejected by the authorization\ncomponent's own trap.\n\n\23\23 Data model\n\n- `SubjectId` and `AttendanceId` are `Nat` counters, unique per owner.\n- `DateKey` is a calendar date in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` form.\n- `ColourHex` is the user-chosen tab colour, e.g. `#F4A261`.\n- `AttendanceStatus` is one of `#present`, `#absent`, `#classCancelled`.\n- `createdAt` and `updatedAt` are nanosecond timestamps (`Int`).\n\n\23\23 Methods\n\n\23\23\23 `createSubject(name : Text, colour : ColourHex) : async SubjectView`\n\nCreates a subject owned by the caller and returns its view\n(`{ id; name; colour; createdAt }`). Update call.\n\n\23\23\23 `listSubjects() : async [SubjectView]`\n\nReturns the caller's subjects, newest first. Query call.\n\n\23\23\23 `deleteSubject(id : SubjectId) : async ?SubjectError`\n\nDeletes one of the caller's subjects. Returns `null` on success, or\n`?#notFound(id)` when no such subject exists and `?#notAuthorized` when it\nbelongs to someone else. Update call. Deleting a subject does not remove its\nattendance records.\n\n\23\23\23 `deleteSubjectWithAttendance(id : SubjectId) : async ?SubjectError`\n\nDeletes one of the caller's subjects together with every attendance record that\nbelongs to it. Returns `null` on success, or `?#notFound(id)` /\n`?#notAuthorized` exactly like `deleteSubject`. Update call. Destructive and not\nidempotent: a second call for the same id returns `?#notFound(id)`.\n\n\23\23\23 `recordAttendance(subjectId : SubjectId, date : DateKey, status : AttendanceStatus) : async Result<AttendanceView, AttendanceError>`\n\nRecords attendance for one of the caller's subjects on `date`. When a record\nalready exists for that subject and date it is updated in place, so repeated\ncalls for the same date are idempotent and safe to retry. Returns `#ok` with the\nstored view (`{ id; subjectId; date; status; updatedAt }`), or\n`#err(#subjectNotFound(subjectId))` when `subjectId` does not exist or is not\nowned by the caller. Update call.\n\n\23\23\23 `listAttendance(subjectId : SubjectId) : async [AttendanceView]`\n\nReturns the caller's attendance records for a subject, newest date first. Query\ncall.\n\n\23\23\23 `deleteAttendance(id : AttendanceId) : async ?AttendanceError`\n\nDeletes one of the caller's attendance records. Returns `null` on success, or\n`?#notFound(id)` / `?#notAuthorized`. Update call. Destructive and not\nidempotent: a second call for the same id returns `?#notFound(id)`.\n\n\23\23\23 `getApiDoc() : async Text`\n\nReturns this document. Query call.\n\n\23\23 Errors and limits\n\nMutations report failures as optional error variants rather than traps, so a\ncaller can branch on them. `#invalidName`, `#invalidColour`, `#invalidDate`, and\n`#subjectNotFound` are reserved for future validation and are not currently\nproduced. There are no pagination limits; listings return every matching record.\n";
    doc;
  };
};
